-report-revenue-and-capital-q4-2025-26-v3-f.pdf","committee":"Cabinet","date":"09/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"Budget Monitoring Report Revenue and Capital Q4 2025 26 v2","url":"http://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices/documents/s170708/budget-monitoring-report-revenue-and-capital-q4-2025-26-v2.pdf","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Board","date":"03/06/2026","key":true},{"title":"TM Outturn 25-26 report - Final","url":"http://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices/documents/s170478/tm-outturn-25-26-report-final.pdf","committee":"Audit Committee","date":"27/05/2026","key":true}],"read_documents":[],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Council","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-09-28","committee":"Children and Young People\u2019s Overview and Scrutiny Sub-Board","time":"3.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-10-08","committee":"Adult Social Care and Health Overview and Scrutiny Sub-Board","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-10-14","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Board","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-10-20","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-11-04","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-11-05","committee":"Adult Social Care and Health Overview and Scrutiny Sub-Board","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-11-11","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Board","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-08-18","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-09-01","committee":"Audit Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-09-03","committee":"Adult Social Care and Health Overview and Scrutiny Sub-Board","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Board","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"},{"date":"2026-09-15","committee":"Cabinet","time":"5.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://www.torbay.gov.uk/DemocraticServices"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Temporary accommodation spending not fully tracked; council cannot currently measure cross-service homelessness costs","lead":"Inability to measure total temporary accommodation spending is a gap in financial visibility; if costs are rising (as suggested by the follow-up status), the council has limited ability to monitor or control them.","iso":"2025-09-08","paper_title":"Annual Internal Audit Report 24-25 - Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://torbay.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s162016/162016.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"HBOP debt recovery suspended for extended period due to staff absence with no recovery monitoring in place","lead":"A significant debt category (HBOP - Housing Benefit Overpayments) has been effectively inactive due to staffing gaps; lack of routine monitoring creates risk that bad debts accumulate without discovery.","iso":"2025-09-08","paper_title":"Annual Internal Audit Report 24-25 - Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://torbay.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s162016/162016.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"SEND deficit requires elimination by end of 2027 under Safety Valve agreement; sector-wide deficit projected to reach \u00a38bn by 2026-27","lead":"This is a mandatory commitment with a fixed deadline; failure to meet the Safety Valve target exposes the council to financial recovery measures; the sector-wide deficit context shows this is a structural funding problem, not a local issue.","iso":"2025-09-08","paper_title":"Annual Internal Audit Report 24-25 - Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://torbay.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s162016/162016.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2025-09-08","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Internal Audit Report 24-25 - Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://torbay.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s162016/162016.pdf","headline":"Temporary accommodation spending not fully tracked; council cannot currently measure cross-service homelessness costs","detail":"The audit found work remains ongoing to 'establish a corporate assessment of spend on homelessness and the provision of accommodation across the organisation' via a shared performance indicator. Currently, spending is tracked separately across services without a consolidated view of total temporary accommodation costs.","category":"demand","matters":"Inability to measure total temporary accommodation spending is a gap in financial visibility; if costs are rising (as suggested by the follow-up status), the council has limited ability to monitor or control them.","figures":"Total spending not quantified","quote":"ongoing examination of options to establish a corporate assessment of spend on homelessness and the provision of accommodation across the organisation in a shared performance reporting indicator on SPAR.","material":true},{"iso":"2025-09-08","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Internal Audit Report 24-25 - Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://torbay.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s162016/162016.pdf","headline":"HBOP debt recovery suspended for extended period due to staff absence with no recovery monitoring in place","detail":"The audit found 'HBOP recovery remains a particular concern, as the one officer working in this area had been absent for a considerable length of time, resulting in a lack of recovery action.' More broadly, 'progress is then not routinely monitored,' meaning bad debts and payment arrangements are not tracked.","category":"audit","matters":"A significant debt category (HBOP - Housing Benefit Overpayments) has been effectively inactive due to staffing gaps; lack of routine monitoring creates risk that bad debts accumulate without discovery.","figures":"Not quantified","quote":"HBOP recovery remains a particular concern, as the one officer working in this area had been absent for a considerable length of time, resulting in a lack of recovery action.","material":true},{"iso":"2025-09-08","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Internal Audit Report 24-25 - Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://torbay.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s162016/162016.pdf","headline":"SEND deficit requires elimination by end of 2027 under Safety Valve agreement; sector-wide deficit projected to reach \u00a38bn by 2026-27","detail":"Torbay is subject to a Safety Valve agreement requiring it to achieve a 'positive in year balance' on the Dedicated Schools Grant deficit 'by the end of 2027.' The audit notes that 'the nationwide SEND deficit currently exceeds \u00a33 billion, projected to rise to \u00a38 billion in 2026-27, presenting significant risks to Council's,' indicating systemic underfunding.","category":"demand","matters":"This is a mandatory commitment with a fixed deadline; failure to meet the Safety Valve target exposes the council to financial recovery measures; the sector-wide deficit context shows this is a structural funding problem, not a local issue.","figures":"National SEND deficit: \u00a33bn rising to \u00a38bn by 2026-27; Torbay deadline: 31 March 2028","quote":"The Council is responsible for implementing a Dedicated Schools Grant (DSG) management plan to control and reduce its cumulative deficit, ensuring a positive in year balance by the end of 2027... A recent CIPFA and ALATS article stated that the nationwide SEND deficit currently exceeds \u00a33 billion, projected to rise to \u00a38 billion in 2026-27, presenting significant risks to Council's.","material":true},{"iso":"2025-09-08","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"Annual Internal Audit Report 24-25 - Audit Committee","paper_url":"https://torbay.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s162016/162016.pdf","headline":"Home-to-school transport spending increased 104% since 2018-19 with minimal increase in actual service use","detail":"The audit reports 'The H2S cost has increased expeditiously since 2018-19, with the Council seeing an increase of 104% in spend with a minimal increase in service use.' A project has been established to address this, but the cost explosion remains unexplained.","category":"overspend","matters":"A 104% cost increase in an essential service with no corresponding growth in take-up indicates either inefficiency, cost inflation, or service scope creep; this represents a major unfunded budget pressure on the council.","figures":"104% increase in H2S spend since 2018-19; minimal increase in service use","quote":"The H2S cost has increased expeditiously since 2018-19, with the Council seeing an increase of 104% in spend with a minimal increase in service use.","material":true},{"iso":"2025-09-08","committee":"Audit Committee","paper_title":"ASC Risk Assurance Report","paper_url":"https://torbay.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s162026/162026.pdf","headline":"Adult Social Care services received a Limited audit opinion from ASW Assurance in 2024/25.","detail":"The Head of Internal Audit at ASW Assurance provided an overall 'Limited' opinion for audit work conducted during 2024/25, based on audits of Deprivation of Liberty Safeguards and Advocacy. This represents a significant control concern in a material service area.","category":"audit","matters":"Adult Social Care represents approximately 30% of the council's net budget, so a Limited audit opinion indicates significant governance or control weaknesses in a third of the council's finances, which directly affects lending decisions and council financial resilience.","figures":"approximately 30% of the Council's overall net budget for 2025/26","quote":"The Head of Internal Audit's opinion, as presented to TSDFT at its Audit and Risk Committee held in June 2025, provided an overall 'Limited' opinion.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-23"},"name":"Torbay UA","findings_total":31,"news_drafts_total":3}}